Advanced Fluid Mechanics — MIT 2.25, Fall 2013 (@fd-mit225: 0, is #reference, #part-of @fd-sources) { r_1ZVEYBFSRC755ASSQ2X87MD8VZ
Gareth McKinley. MIT 2.25 Advanced Fluid Mechanics, Fall 2013, graduate. [Course and topic materials](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-25-advanced-fluid-mechanics-fall-2013/) · [Syllabus](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-25-advanced-fluid-mechanics-fall-2013/pages/syllabus/).

Work the full public progression, substantial problems and the available examinations before consulting their solutions. The course develops continuum balances, statics, inviscid and viscous flow, similarity, lubrication, potential flow, vorticity, boundary layers and interfaces. Its aim is fluent reasoning from physical principles.

The public archive includes problem sets, solutions and exams; it is not a claim that all classroom lectures are recorded. The syllabus assigns Shapiro–Sonin problems discussed in tutorials rather than submitted as ordinary homework. MIT OCW uses CC BY-NC-SA with separately credited exceptions and external readings. The archive's 2013 materials and current MITx courses are distinct resources.

**Return:** [Fluid dynamics sources — books, courses, methods and physical evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_3Y3TVV9VQAB50M2ZSECK5JTYVG).
